   Conf on Climate Changes, Global Warming, Biological Programs/1st WSEAS
   Int Conf on Natural Hazards, Bucharest, ROMANIA, NOV 07-09, 2008},
Organization = {WSEAS},
Abstract = {Radon is colourless gas, with high toxicity for lung tissue. Radon is
   the second leading cause of lung cancer, and a serious occupational and
   public health concern. Different techniques are used to measure radon
   concentration at working environment. In this study, Track etch
   detectors were used to determine the radon levels at different working
   environment areas at segregation line, baling area, residual area and
   administration area at a Materials Recycling Facility (MRF). Radon
   radiation doses were also estimated. Simple remediation methods to
   reduce the radon concentration were recommended to the operator.
   Although the radon concentration and radon doses were reduced as result
   of remedial measures that were taken by the operator, the resultant data
   clearly indicated that simple remedial measures can be a powerful tool
   to reduce radon concentration.},
