Note = {2nd International Conference on Innovation, Communication and
   Engineering (ICICE), Qingdao, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 26-NOV 01, 2013},
Organization = {China Univ Petr; Taiwanese Inst Knowledge Innovat},
Abstract = {At present, the renewable energy attracts people's more attentions as
   the environment is becoming worse and supply of energy is getting
   tenser. Wind power is not only clean but also more nature in technology
   and able to be explored in larger scale compared with other type of
   renewable energy. Therefore, it is being acclaimed and emphasized by
   most nations. In this study, considering NACA0008 airfoil of small
   H-type vertical axis wind turbine, the effects of blade support point,
   rotating speed and wind velocity on the structural strength and
   deformation of the airfoil are investigated. The performance of NACA0008
   airfoil is numerically studied. Further, the lifting and drag forces on
   the airfoil are presented in approximate formula. Moreover, the force
   applied to due to the coupled effect of wind velocity and rotating speed
   is calculated by using the ANSYS software. It is discovered that when
   the ratio of distance between support position with the blade and blade
   height is about 22.7\%, the deformation of blade and stress are minimum.
   In addition, the simple and approximated method is also presented.
   Comparing the numerical results of the presented and approximated
   methods, the error of the approximated method is about 2\%.},
