Title = {Research on the Plastic Debris in the Pacific Ocean},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 4TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON ENVIRONMENTAL
   TECHNOLOGY AND KNOWLEDGE TRANSFER},
Year = {2012},
Pages = {411-417},
Note = {4th International Conference on Environmental Technology and Knowledge
   Transfer, Hefei, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 24-25, 2012},
Organization = {Hefei Univ; Univ Rostock; State Univ N Carolina; Hefei Assoc Sci \&
   Technol; Anhui Environm Sci Soc},
Abstract = {The deleterious effect of the plastic debris mass in the Great Pacific
   Ocean is coming to light. We pay close attention to the process about
   how the plastic debris affects human being in order to arouse people's
   vigilance before it becomes too serious to deal with. Because of the
   excessive use of the plastic, the massive amount of the garbage patch
   will increase, the degradation of the plastic will release toxic
   chemicals which will go into the human body through the food chain.
   In this article, our focal point is the process about how the plastic
   affects human being. A comprehensive model is built to describe the
   process. The process contains 4 steps, for each step we build a
   sub-model to describe and evaluate the effects. As to step 1, we build a
   grey dynamic prediction model to predict the number of plastic produced
   by human being. The result shows that 180.3 million tons of plastic will
   be discarded into the ocean until 2015 if no action is taken. Thus it
   will cause great pollution to the marine ecology system and affects the
   human being's life. Next, a computer simulation model was carried out to
   show the formation of the Great Pacific Ocean garbage patch. Because of
   the effect of the ocean currents, the plastic{''} floating on the
   surface of the ocean will finally flow into the center of the swirl and
   at last form a garbage patch. We also calculate that all of the plastic
   produced in 2015 will take the nature nearly 61.7 years to purify.Then,
   in order to study the degradation of the plastic, we use SPSS for the
   multiple :regression analysis. and then we can get the results that the
   average molecular weight of plastic will change under different
   temperature and different relative humidity with the ultraviolet light
   (315nm) treatment. Thus we can get the information of the degradation
   because the rate of the plastic degradation can be evaluated by the
   average molecular weight. Finally we use the food chain model to
   evaluate the way about how the plastic affects marine ecology.Of course,
   our model needs future scientific research in some aspects: From start
   to finish, we stick to the Scientific literatures. The data used in our
   model all comes from reliable websites source. According to our model,
   we suggest that the government should take measures to reduce the
   pollution of the plastic, our study has indicated that the garbage patch
   is harmful to human being and the marine ecology},
