   Future, Taichung, TAIWAN, NOV 13-16, 2018},
Organization = {ISHS, Div Hort Human Hlth; ISHS, Working Grp Hort Therapy},
Abstract = {Some research shown that environments of leisure farms have beneficial
   impacts on physiological and psychological health - attention
   restorative, autonomic arousal and stress reduction, for example. Most
   research focuses on the features of natural environments such as
   naturalness, elements, beauty and so on, but seldom discusses the
   influences of landscape color and their physical-psychological benefits.
   There are lots of studies on the influence of color on psychology and
   physiology, but not so many studies on what effect environmental colors
   have on both of psychological and physical benefits. Consequently, this
   study attempt to figure out what benefits and impact the composition of
   environmental colors has on psychological and physical health.
   Experiments were conducted in 11 sites of different leisure farms and
   429 subjects were collected with 11 pictures of landscapes of these
   leisure farms. The physiological health indicators used in this study
   are heart rate, electroencephalography and electromyography. The
   psychological measurements are attention restorative and emotional
   experience. This study used the RBG color model to analyze the
   composition of RBG's percentage of farms' landscapes. This study found
   percentage of red color has a negative relation to alpha waves of right
   brain; percentage of green color has a positive relation to attention
   restorative and electromyography; percentage of blue color has a
   negative relation to electromyography. The result proved the percentages
   of RGB might be a factor in the psychological and physical health impact
   of leisure farms.},
