   (ISCDC), Cairo, EGYPT, DEC 02-04, 2015},
Abstract = {Considering the Cairene context and its urban extensions, this paper
   hypothesizes that planned urban districts are becoming less suitable for
   children to walk to school. A questionnaire was sent to parents of
   children in grades 4, 5 and 6 of 3 schools; one in each of
   Dokki/Mohandeseen (n=406), Madinet Nasr (n=124) and 6th of October City
   (n=98) to explore the mode by which students travel to school and the
   different variables affecting the parental perception and decision.
   Results showed that active school travel is much less practiced in new
   cities than in the inner city districts with percentages 35.3\% in
   Dokki, 40.9\% in Madinet Nasr and 12.5\% in October. (C) 2016 The
