   Dispersion Modelling for Regulatory Purposes, ROUEN, FRANCE, OCT 11-14,
   1999},
Abstract = {This paper presents the basic principles of the method of calculating
   air pollution from road traffic in an urban built-up area. The algorithm
   of the method is based on the numerical integration of stationary
   two-dimensional partial differential equations of turbulent diffusion,
   with boundary conditions for the street canyons. The method consists of
   two modules: KALIB and STREETS, which calculate the distribution of
   pollutant concentration ill a street canyon; and GRID and GRIDMAX, which
   calculate the distribution of pollutant concentration in the free
   atmosphere. The output of the method is given in numerical and graphical
   form.},
