Abstract = {This paper summarises the main aspects of the ARIPAR methodology whose
   steps have been applied in quantifying major accident risks due to
   processing, storing and transporting dangerous substances in the Ravenna
   (Italy) area, where a densely populated town lives near a large complex
   of chemical and petrochemical plants. The attention is chiefly addressed
   to describe as the results of a quantified area risk analysis can
   support, and in the specific case have supported, local administrations
   in establishing priorities of structural interventions and in assuming
   decisions of land-use control and urban planning.},
