   Greece; MITOS SA},
Abstract = {The PC version of the stormwater runoff model ILLUDAS was used to
   simulate quantity of urban stormwater runoff in four sites in South
   Florida, each with a specific predominant land use (i.e., low density
   residential, high density residential, highway and commercial).
   Seventy-two storm events were used for model calibration and 26
   independent rainfall events were used for model verification. Calibrated
   input parameters are presented with the objective of providing modelers
   with a way to select appropriate input parameters to be used in similar
   studies. Predicted hydrographs by this model compared well with measured
   ones.},
