   INTERDISCIPLINARY TASK, VOLS 1-3},
Year = {2002},
Pages = {251-259},
Note = {30th IAHS World Congress on Housing, UNIV COIMBRA, COIMBRA, PORTUGAL,
   SEP 09-13, 2002},
Organization = {Int Assoc Housing Sci},
Abstract = {This paper describes a research project which investigated the
   implications of integrating light steel frame systems into the design of
   innovative houses for the current English housing market. A housing
   design project was set for students of architecture; their interaction
   with the construction system was evaluated and compared with the
   experiences of practitioners in the construction industry. The
   construction system was found to have an impact at urban, layout and
   detail levels of the design process, and to affect the resultant
   product. Implications are drawn for the design, construction and
   marketing of houses built with light steel frame.},
