Abstract = {Cities with their suburbs have long become the subject to be studied by
   academic community. The city is a symbol of a society complexity.
   Various spatial factors of the city milieu can generate a feeling of
   insecurity. The paper investigates to what extent Yekaterinburg city
   residents find their city safe. The survey embraces one hundred and ten
   Yekaterinburg old-timers. The integrated image of the ``safe city{''}
   includes the following factors: townspeople want to trust those who live
   in the same city; the city should possess protectability features and be
   seen as ``home{''} by natives. (C) 2013 The Authors. Published by
