   Unilever Plc; Hamdard Fdn Pakistan; Univ Glasgow; Univ Bradford},
Abstract = {Over the last century the Indus River in Pakistan has become an almost
   fully managed river. With water management, settlement and irrigation
   the nature of the flood risks have changed. Low to medium flooding of
   the river can he controlled. But high floods can produce water levels
   above those assumed in the design of the control structures on the
   river. A new type of vulnerability is produced that requires a planned
   response. The nature of this response is described.},
