   Geol; Yunnan Bureau Geol; Mineral Resources Explorat \& Dev; K C Wong
   Educ Fdn},
Abstract = {With the development of urbanization, groundwater contamination has
   become important issues for the urban groundwater supply. This study has
   investigated the chemical characteristics and the contamination of
   groundwater in relation to urbanization. The characteristics of chemical
   component of groundwater are analyzed, summed and classified. The
   results show that: (1) There are rapidly increase for the concentration
   of Cl-, as well as SO4- in groundwater from 1989 to 2002 and 2003; (2)
   Groundwater chemistry is more influenced by urbanization than by aquifer
   rock type; (3) The main cause for Cl- increasing in fracture-karst water
   is leaching from a waste dump by atmospheric precipitation.},
