   BUILDING ENVELOPES IN CHINA},
Booktitle = {FIFTH INTERNATIONAL WORKSHOP ON ENERGY AND ENVIRONMENT OF RESIDENTIAL
   BUILDINGS AND THIRD INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON BUILT ENVIRONMENT AND
   PUBLIC HEALTH, VOL I AND II, PROCEEDINGS},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {1470-1477},
Note = {5th International Workshop on Energy and Environment of Residential
   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {In this paper, affecting factors on thermal load characteristics of
   residential building envelopes in China is focused. The location of an
   analytical residential building model is selected in Beijing area. Some
   affecting factors of building pattern on summer cooling load of
   residential building envelopes are selected, such as orientation of
   buildings, area ratio of window to wall, characteristics of window,
   dimensions of shade, characteristics of external wall, characteristics
   of roof etc.. EnergyPlus software issued by U.S.A is employed to do the
   simulation of building cooling load in summer. The effect analysis of
   different combination of all affecting factors has been done by
   orthogonal experimental method. From this work, the changing trend of
   cooling load of a typical residential building with the change of each
   affecting factor can be obtained and presented. The optimal combination
   scheme of the affecting factors with the minimum building cooling load
   can also be obtained. Furthermore, the affecting notability of each
   affecting factor can be analyzed and selected. These works are very
   important to give us a guidance to do a building design that has the
   characteristics of high energy efficiency and low energy consumption.
   In this paper, a comparison analysis of summer cooling load among three
   typical residential room patterns in China has been also done.},
