   18-22, 1992},
Abstract = {A computer code is presented to determine the concentration
   distributions due to vehicle emissions in urban or rural areas. The
   following factors have been taken into consideration: (i) the built-up
   area and terrain height; (ii) meteorological conditions (wind,
   stability, precipitation); and (iii) the traffic mix and flow along
   individual street segments. The data input is managed by means of menu
   techniques. Output of the computation are plots of the wind-field and
   contour area plots of `he pollutants CO, NO, and NC as well as SO2, Pb
   and soot. In this paper a comparison between measurements and
   computations, as well as a sensitivity analysis with respect to the
   input data, is given for CO.},
