Note = {2024 International Conference on Geographic Perspectives on Climate
   Change Mitigation in Urban and Rural Environments-GCUE, Lecce, ITALY,
   JUN 25-27, 2024},
Organization = {University of Salento},
Abstract = {Sustainability is a central focus across various fields and is
   recognized as a key driver for achieving sustainable development.
   Education, in particular, plays a vital role in this effort, as many
   sustainable development initiatives emphasize its importance. This
   research aims to promote innovative strategies for sustainable school
   design, specifically targeting the environment of Al-Mreigha Mixed Basic
   School in Ma'an, Jordan, through the lens of computational architecture.
   The study is divided into two main areas of focus. First, it identifies
   and addresses concerns related to the comfort of school
   occupants-thermal, visual, and acoustic comfort-using both
   questionnaires and interviews. Second, it evaluates the impact of
   proposed sustainability measures on the school's operational efficiency
   through the use of simulation software, such as Design Builder, as a
   computational architectural tool. The research explores four design
   alternatives: upgrading wall insulation, adding highly efficient ceiling
   insulation, modifying glazing types, and implementing shading devices.
   Simulations reveal varying effects on temperature regulation, heat
   gains, and energy consumption, highlighting how computational approaches
   can optimize design decisions. The discussion emphasizes the importance
   of optimal insulation, shading solutions, and energy-efficient lighting,
   showcasing how computational architecture can facilitate sustainable
   design outcomes.},
